{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkRJfqiA7VUsaiTvRZZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FJ3HhworTbMQKZ3PUPEXpp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/var/folders/XX/XXXX/T/skilleval-golden-01-2-f61eugbb/.eval-home/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-g9--dhv-jzj5ljd5nywv14y31hm0000gn-T-skilleval-golden-01-2-f61eugbb/memory/worktree_jam_fix.md","content":"---\nname: worktree_jam_fix\ndescription: Procedure to unstick jammed git worktrees without rediscovery\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWhen a git worktree is jammed (operations hang), follow this procedure:\n\n1. `git status` to see what operation is held up\n2. Locate `index.lock` file in the worktree\n3. Identify the PID that owns the lock file: `lsof | grep index.lock` or check the file contents\n4. Kill the blocking process: `kill -9 <pid>`\n5. Prune the stale worktree entry: `git worktree prune`\n\n**Why:** This has recurred 3+ times in a week; agents rediscovering the fix each session is expensive.\n\n**How to apply:** When encountering a hung git operation in a worktree, skip deep diagnosis and apply this procedure directly. If an agent is working with worktrees, reference this before they waste tokens investigating.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6909,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6909},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"82291441-7134-4c38-b84f-009d8cb52b9c","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:52:41.716Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkRHiJ2XnWw17fFhhJJ"}
